#6918
Rue de Tethyr~
Travelling down this street, you are amazed and bewildered by the extravagance
to which the villagers have gone in paving their streets.  Emeralds, sapphires,
diamonds, rubies and gemstones of every kind and size have been used as paving
stones.  Villagers think nothing of walking across them, but you notice many of
the visitors walking as if on eggshells in a vain attempt to avoid stepping on
any valuable stones.  Occasionally, a visitor stops and tries to remove one of
the paving stones then, looking around sheepishly, continues on his way.~
