#6953
Maison de Jean-Pierre~
You have entered Jean-Pierre's house.  Portraits of people you believe must
be relatives from many generations form the focal point of his house.  Each
one is expertly painted and in an elaborate gold frame.  The furniture is 
made of dark, fancifully sculptured wood, overlaid in strategic places to
add to its aesthetic nature without being overly dramatic.  If it weren't
for the extreme extravagance of the village, you would consider this to be
an absurd show of wealth and an attempt to flaunt it in your face.  Taking
the great wealth of the city into consideration, it seems actually to be 
more conservative than you would expect.~
69 ROOM_NO_CASTLE|ROOM_NO_RIP|ROOM_INDOORS SECT_CITY
DDIR_SOUTH
Rue d'Anasazi ~
~
0 -1 6913
S

#6954
Maison d'Antoinette~
Antoinette's house is full of knick knacks, except that these particular ones
are of great value.  The walls are covered with small shelves for displaying
each of them in elegant fashion.  The furniture is quite old, but in great
condition nonetheless.  She has large, expensive rugs lying on the floors.
The soft smell of perfume fills the air.~
