#6958
Maison d'Henri~
Entering the home of Henri, you notice a heavy use of straight lines and
angles in the architecture.  Everything in the house as well as the house
itself is designed entirely of straight lines and angles.  The floor, in
keeping with this design scheme, has no rug but consists of hardwood strips
interspersed with seemingly random segments of gold and silver.  As you study
it more intensely, you see an intricate mathematical design in the placement
of each board, each segment of gold or silver, and even in the direction of
the grain and hue of the stain in the wood.  It obviously took intense
planning to lay out the floor. The furniture is placed with care so as not
to disturb the mathematical design, and so, enhances it.~
69 ROOM_NO_CASTLE|ROOM_NO_RIP|ROOM_INDOORS SECT_CITY
